Filters on locators

Parten child relation 
The .filter() method allows you to narrow down a list of elements based on what is inside them

a. hasText - Simple text matching
.filter({ hasText: "example" })

b. has - Filter elements having a child with role/link
.filter({ has: locator.getByRole('link', { name: 'xyz' }) })

c. hasNot - Exclude elements having unwanted child
.filter({ hasNot: locator.getByRole('link', { name: 'abc' }) })

d. .and() operator - when we need to match both locators condition at the same time 
page.locator('button').and(page.getByText('Submit'))

locator chaining -  find element within element [use when need to find the child locator]
page.locator('div').getByRole('button') 
but .and find same element with 2 attribute

e. .or operator - locator matches any of the element 
page.locator('button').or(page.getByText('Login'))

Usage 
.and() -> When one locator is too broad and you need to narrow it down.
.or() -> When the element might appear in different forms/texts. 
chaining -> Need to find child
